Structure of the hypervisor MD
------------------------------

An MD is a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG): the nodes are joined by arcs.
An arc goes from a node to another node.
A "fwd" arc goes down the graph, a "back" arc goes up.
Every "fwd" arc has a "back" arc in the node it points to.
The format is explained in
https://unix0.cc/2026/07/15/sun4v-machine-description-part-1/

This table shows, for each node type, its arcs and its properties, as the blobs
have them.
There is one node of each type, so an arc names a type.
(pci) means: only in the pci MD.
The node names are those of the table above.
tests/full/md/internal/refdoc.sh checks the table against md/*/1up-hv.bin of
legion and pci.

